# o365pop — AI Context

> Read this file at the start of every conversation or task. It is the map; the other docs are the territory.

---

## What Is o365pop

Local LibreELEC daemon that lets vintage POP/SMTP clients (Entourage 2008) talk to Microsoft 365. WireGuard is the security layer. POP3 and SMTP stay 1998-compatible (no TLS, USER/PASS, AUTH LOGIN). Celery owns Graph sync and Fido-style tossing. `popd` / `smtpd` only speak the wire protocols.

---

## Architecture

```
Entourage --WG--> popd/smtpd --fs--> maildir/spool
                      ^
Celery worker/beat ---+--> tosser --> graph (httpx) --> Microsoft 365
                      +--> sqlite (account, tossed-index, chat_map)
```

- **Tech stack:** Python 3.14 package, SQLite, Celery + Redis, httpx + MSAL, aiosmtpd, Twisted POP3, maildir
- **Key decisions:** Fido tosser; daemons never call Graph; cleartext POP/SMTP on the WG bind; one mailbox; no web UI
- **Data:** `MailboxAccount`, `SyncSession`, `TossedMessage`, `ChatMap`; maildir inbound; spool outbound
- **Full details:** `docs/architecture/SAO.md` (Design Principles + §§1–16). SAO §17 (agents) is N/A.

